<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tanda (Bengal)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tanda was a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaur">Gaur</a> in present-day Malda district, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bengal">West Bengal</a>. Sulaiman Khan Karrani made it the capital of the Bengal Sultanate in the 1560s, and it remained the seat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal-subah">Mughal Bengal</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajmahal">Rajmahal</a> replaced it in 1595. It was later abandoned and destroyed by the shifting course of the Ganges, and no ruins survive.</p></div>
